#6404
Entranceway to the Monastery~
   You stand in the entranceway of the monastery, a plain room of
whitewashed walls and polished wooden floor where visitors leave their
boots in neat rows.  To the east a hallway leads into the rest of the
monastery and the practice grounds beyond.  From the south comes
chanting and the low hum of monks at prayer.  The archway leads west.
