#6413
A Monk's Cell~
   A monk's private quarters are called a cell, and from the sparseness
of its furnishings you can easily guess why.  A small cot is the only
real piece of furniture; a folded blanket, a prayer mat and a single
candle stub complete the room's comforts.  The plain stone walls are
swept spotless.  A heavy curtain to the south leads back to the hallway.
~
